 "text": "Taliesin is a Welsh hero and a great bard. His work is dated to the sixth century. He was said to hold earlier lives. First he was the boy Gwion, a servant to the goddess Ceridwen. Ceridwen brewed a magic drink for her son Afagddu. A drop fell on Gwion and he ate it and took in the power meant for the son. Gwion fled and took many forms. At last Ceridwen ate him and bore him again. A lord named Elphin raised the child as Taliesan. Taliesan grew to be the wisest poet in the land. He could see across the veil into the Otherworld.",
